{ Which piece needs improvement before b4? What exact pawn weakness would b5 create? Name the structure and one resource for the other side. ANSWER: The c-file is half-open for White and the black c6 pawn can become a target after b4-b5. Your queenside minority tries to create a weakness, not a passed pawn immediately. Coordinate a rook on b1 or c1, prepare b4, and assess b5. If ...cxb5, examine the isolated d-pawn or weak c-file squares; if ...c5, recalculate the central structure. Black: Black seeks ...Ne4, kingside activity and the freeing ...c5. If those threats are urgent, a slow pawn plan may be too slow. } *

