{ Which square is directly in front of the isolated pawn? Can you occupy it safely? Name the structure and one resource for the other side. ANSWER: Black's d-pawn has no friendly c- or e-pawn to support it. It controls central squares, so it is not simply a free target. Restrain its advance, blockade with a suitable piece, and exchange active attacking pieces when favorable. Attack the pawn only after your king and pieces are coordinated. Black: Black wants ...d4 or an initiative before the position simplifies. A poorly timed pawn capture can release all of Black's pieces. } *

