{ Which trade favors the blockader? What would have to change for d5 to work? Name the structure and one resource for the other side. ANSWER: White has an isolated d4 pawn and open central lines. The pawn offers space and activity but can become an endgame burden. Use active bishops and rooks, keep useful attacking pieces, and prepare d5 if it opens the position favorably. Make the opponent defend threats before they can blockade. Black: Black wants a stable blockade and favorable piece exchanges. Avoid trading into a passive ending simply because it reduces the material. } *

