{ If ...d4 is played, which square and pawn become vulnerable? Name the structure and one resource for the other side. ANSWER: The adjacent black c5 and d5 pawns lack friendly pawns on the neighboring outer files. Together they control useful central squares; after one advances, the other may become weak. For the side facing them, pressure both pawns and provoke a concession without allowing a strong advance. For the side owning them, keep activity and choose the right moment to push. Black: One careless exchange can turn the pair into a strong passed pawn rather than a weakness. Calculate recaptures before celebrating a structural target. } *

