{ Why does a4 matter here? Which move opens the bishop that can recover c4? Name the structure and one resource for the other side. ANSWER: Black has captured on c4 and White has played a4. The immediate structural battle concerns whether ...b5 can hold the extra pawn. Develop e3 and Bxc4 when safe. Do not replace useful development with queen moves just to regain the pawn one move sooner. Black: Black can counter in the center while you recover c4. The later e4 break must be supported against pins and exchanges. } *

