{ Which pawn break is realistic for each side? Which knight has the clearest route to a better square? Name the structure and one resource for the other side. ANSWER: White's d5 and e4 pawns face Black's d6 and e5 pawns. The center is closed, but pawn breaks can reopen it. Improve the least active minor piece and identify a useful break. Queenside space is valuable only if it creates entry squares or targets. Keep the fianchetto bishop's defensive role in mind. Black: Black can prepare kingside activity or queenside breaks. The exact knight placements decide whether ...f5 or ...b5 is feasible. } *

