{ What does Nb3 attack? Why is e3 tactically different from a quiet QGD e3 move? Name the structure and one resource for the other side. ANSWER: The d4 pawn limits your pieces and creates tactics on e3 and along the d-file. White's extra e5 pawn does not remove those threats. Nbd2-b3 targets d4. Address pins first, and return material if needed to simplify safely. Know the en-passant detail in the e4 line. Black: Black seeks fast development, ...Bg4, and attacks while your king is central. Greedy bishop captures can allow a dangerous passed pawn. } *

