{ Which break would free Black's position? Can it be prevented usefully, or should you prepare to meet it? Name the structure and one resource for the other side. ANSWER: Black keeps pawns on a6, b6, d6 and e6 behind compact pieces. White has more space, but that space can become vulnerable if overextended. Improve pieces and watch ...b5 and ...d5. Do not attack a compact position by creating more weak pawns than targets. Black: Black waits for a central or queenside break that activates several pieces at once. A quiet move may be a tactical preparation. } *

